 resilience and technical competence, but communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education. Candidate C has strong situational awareness, leadership, but show-off, not open to new ideas. Which is stronger overall? We need to argue.\n\nWe could ask for more info about crew cooperation for Candidate C (e.g., how does show-off affect crew). Or ask about Candidate D's hot temper effect. But we need to respond now.\n\nWe could challenge Agent 1's claim that \"positive crew atmosphere may offset issues\" by pointing out that communication difficulty and egocentric attitude are serious for crew cooperation, especially long-haul flights. Also note that Candidate C's leadership and anticipation may outweigh attitude concerns. So we maintain vote for Candidate C, providing reasoning.\n\nWe should reference Agent 1's points and our own facts. Provide evidence: Candidate C anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, leadership. Concerns: show-off, not open to new ideas. Argue that these concerns are less safety-critical than communication issues of A, which could directly affect cockpit coordination. Also note that A not willing to further education may hinder adaptability.\n\nThus we keep vote for Candidate C.\n\nWe need to output PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON.\n\nLet's craft."}
